# Life 2 arrival (life/arrival.js, design/data/arrival.toml, the `arrival` anchor of design/data/anchors.toml). Expect:
# "Arrival: x y z (grounded) ..." (within `search` blocks of the anchor, once grounded, about 20 s after start; a
# "provisional" line only on a fresh world), then a reborn bot lands within 3 blocks of it, on Jura's safe rim (its
# /ttlregion says zone rim) and not in Tempest, standing on dry ground, and is still alive 10 s later (area magicule there is 500;
# the forest ahead is lethal for a fresh soul; the arrival grace of arrival.toml keeps the rim's Blade Tigers and Barghests
# from killing it, but they still shove it: after 10 s it only has to be within 32 blocks). Any "ttl: ..." line is a failure.
# tests/ingame/lerfing.rcon checks the anchor itself against Lerfing's stored chunks (needs the import).
ttl arrival
# Wild Tensura direwolves spawn on the safe rim round the arrival (three stood within 16 blocks of it on 19/11); their
# attacks knocked the reborn bot 3 and 36 blocks off the point (test-all 10:49 and 12:19). Clear them first.
execute in minecraft:overworld positioned ${anchor:arrival.x} 72 ${anchor:arrival.z} run kill @e[type=tensura:direwolf,distance=..96]
ttlbot spawn TtlBotArrival
@sleep 2
kill TtlBotArrival
execute as TtlBotArrival run ttl wish knowledge
execute as TtlBotArrival run ttl choose slime
@sleep 2
ttl inspect TtlBotArrival
ttl arrival expect TtlBotArrival near 3
# On the rim, not in the dark band or the core ("zone rim (safe)" on Lerfing's stored biomes, "zone ring 'rim' ..." from the
# generator's ring maths), and not in or over water or lava.
@expect 5 zone (rim|ring 'rim') :: ttlregion TtlBotArrival
@expect 5 Test passed :: execute as TtlBotArrival at @s unless block ~ ~ ~ minecraft:water unless block ~ ~-1 ~ minecraft:water unless block ~ ~-1 ~ minecraft:lava
@sleep 10
ttl arrival expect TtlBotArrival alive
ttl arrival expect TtlBotArrival near 32
ttl reset TtlBotArrival
ttlbot remove TtlBotArrival
